      "narration": "Around the first century, Aksum rose to dominate the region. They were savvy merchants, minting their own gold coins to turn local power into international status. These coins traveled across the Red Sea, marking Aksum as a major player in global trade. It was a bold move that put them firmly on the map. They controlled the flow of goods.",
